      "definition": "Jayanandipāda, the siddha to whom the manuscript attributes song 46 (jayanandīpādānāṃ, written before the song). He names himself Jaanandi in its last line (5b). Munidatta calls him one who has gained the higher knowledges (cp.46.m1). The Tibetan has dza yA nan+de in the heading, dza ya nan+ti in the line and dza ya nan+ta in the comment.",
      "symbolicImage": "",
      "symbolicReadings": [],
      "forbiddenInLine": [],
      "rationale": "The poet of song 46 has no entry; like the other siddhas he is kept in source form, with the bhaṇitā form Jaanandi and the plain Jayanandi as variants for the reviewer to choose between."
    },
