      ],
      "definition": "Śabarī, the name of the rāga (melodic mode) to which song 46 is sung, given in its heading; the same word names a woman of the Śabaras, who has her own entry. The Tibetan transcribes it sham+ba rI. The rāga of song 26, printed Śīvarī, has Tibetan sha ba ri and may be the same melody; that is not established.",
      "symbolicImage": "",
      "symbolicReadings": [],
      "forbiddenInLine": [],
      "rationale": "Rāga names have their own keep-source entries (raga beside raga-passion, bangala beside pl-banga); 'sabari' is the Śabara woman of song 28, with Nairātmā readings and forbidden words, so the heading should not link to it. The match only takes শবরী after রাগ."
    },
