        }
      ],
      "definition": "To burn or be burnt (Old Bengali dāṭai, which Munidatta renders dagdha, 'burnt'; Tibetan tshig pa). Song 46 (3a) says it is not burnt, not wetted and not cut, a stock Indian triad for the indestructible (compare the Bhagavad Gītā on the self). Munidatta: not burnt by fire, not flooded by water, not cut by a weapon (cp.46.m4).",
      "symbolicImage": "",
      "symbolicReadings": [],
      "forbiddenInLine": [],
      "rationale": "3a turns on three things that cannot happen to the mind freed of delusion; 'cut' already has an entry (cutting), so burning and wetting get entries to keep the triad consistent across line, comment and Tibetan. Whole-word patterns, since দাটই and দগ্ধং are short (দগ্ধ sits inside বিদগ্ধ)."
    },
