      "definition": "To wet or be soaked (Old Bengali timai; compare Sanskrit tim-, 'become wet'; Tibetan gsher, 'wet'). Song 46 (3a) names it between burning and cutting as what cannot happen: it is not burnt, not wetted, not cut. Munidatta has 'it is not to be flooded by water' (cp.46.m4); the Tibetan comment, 'not carried off by water'.",
